# Navigator uses the committed prepared projection

## Pre-work plan

- Context: immutable Renderer/Interactive.Client 0.2.58 is deployed and the generated bundle contains `tryNavigatorEventRangeIntent`, but the formal long body drag still emits `ui:4` without `CoverageIntent`.
- 目標: make the actual pointerdown-frozen navigator path use the same loaded-coverage projection authority that rendered the navigator, then produce a new immutable package for the unchanged real B gate.
- 假設: the visible navigator is rendered from `chartCommittedFrame` prepared `RawData`, while `loadedCoverageSnapshot` decodes only the paired runtime state's unresolved `Data`. When the projection exists only in prepared data, the option is `None` and release falls through to bare `setWindow`.
- Source of truth: 0.2.58 consumer action/gesture/final evidence under `G:\coldfar_py\coldfar-symbolics\temp\agent.daedilus\resident-width-and-edges-0258`, the atomic `(RuntimeState * TaPreparedRendererData)` committed frame, and Renderer source at `7027136ba7d957a026552addbbb28c3d4c8c25cd`.
- Invariant: pointerdown gesture geometry, prepared timeline, loaded-coverage projection, event-time range and purpose come from one committed prepared frame. Runtime envelope data must not replace prepared/resolved data for a rendered interaction.
- Scope: Renderer source/test, Renderer/Interactive versions and direct tests, RFC/SA/SD/WBS/TEST/DevLog/log, package/build/test evidence. Consumer source/count heuristic remain out of scope.
- Acceptance: source RED proves unresolved runtime data plus resolved prepared data; release produces a navigator-purpose intent from prepared authority; package-backed Renderer/Interactive/verifier/BrowserDemo pass; Daedilus same real B sequence reaches local0 without A/D/highlight/Tagging regression.
- 風險: using a newer runtime projection would mix generations; the fix must read only the pointerdown-frozen `dragPreparedData.RawData`, never `runtimeState.Value` or `latestPreparedData`.

